keywords:
  - adversarial robustness
  - vision-language models
  - FGSM
  - PGD
  - gradient saliency
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered, held-out evidence that 3-step PGD's advantage over FGSM on
  Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct at an L-infinity budget of one 8-bit level comes from
  which RGB channel coordinates it perturbs, and that two standard
  clean-gradient rules rank those coordinates below random. Source code is
  MIT-licensed; original synthetic scenes, experimental records, figures and
  research documentation are CC BY 4.0. The draft manuscript (Markdown, HTML
  and PDF versions) is not licensed for reuse; see the README's License
  section for this and other exclusions.
